<description>
**Problem:** The mempool estimator added in #34075 checks mempool health by comparing the weight of transactions removed from our mempool with the weight of recently mined blocks.
`removeForBlock` matches block transactions by txid, which does not commit to witness data.
If a block confirms a lighter witness variant than the one in our mempool, the estimator counts our heavier variant, so the health check can pass even when the matched transactions make up less than 75% of the mined weight.
A heavier mined variant has the opposite effect and understates coverage.
Same-txid witness variants also came up in #35501.

**Fix:** Count each matched transaction's weight from the connected block instead.
`removeForBlock` returns matches in block order, so the estimator can walk the block and the removed entries together.
The new test first records the false healthy result, then the corrected low-coverage result.
#36182 falls back to block policy for combined estimates when the mempool estimator cannot produce an estimate, but a false healthy result never reaches that fallback.
</description>

<commits>
847f90a0d7 test: characterize witness-weight coverage

A transaction ID does not commit to witness data. Record that the estimator counts a heavier local mempool variant and marks the window healthy even though the matching mined transactions fall below the coverage threshold.

7b785e3878 refactor: sum block weight with a loop

Use a coinbase-skipping loop to sum block weight. Continue summing
removed mempool entries separately so coverage values stay the same.

4488d3c452 refactor: sum block coverage in one pass

Walk the connected block and matching mempool entries in one pass.
`removeForBlock` returns those entries in block order. Keep counting
the local variant's weight so the refactor preserves the existing
coverage result.

2acb7962a9 fees: count mined weight in coverage

Transactions with the same txid can have different witnesses in our
mempool and the connected block. Count each match using the mined
variant's weight so the local witness size cannot skew the health check.

Update the statistic comment and `estimatesmartfee` help to describe
the mined weight.
</commits>

